From cb0a5427c2ecf9f486873a3dac2a12f8aee11f41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:28:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media-driver: Add missing include dirs for all 6 "_base"
 platform variants

A real build failed with a fatal "'encode_av1_vdenc_pipeline_adapter_xe_lpm_plus_base.h'
file not found" compiling the AV1 encode pipeline adapter for
Xe_LPM_plus.

This is not a fork-restoration issue -- it's a gap in this session's
own GenerateAndroidBp.py-based Android.bp regeneration. Every
"_base"-suffixed platform variant directory (Xe_LPM_plus_base,
Xe2_LPM_base, Xe_HPG_Base, Xe3P_LPG_base, Xe3P_LPM_base, Xe3_LPM_base)
had its .cpp sources correctly picked up in srcs, but none of their
header-containing subdirectories made it into local_include_dirs --
apparently the tool's include-scraping (reading CXX_INCLUDES from a
single representative flags.make) didn't traverse into any of these
6 directory trees for any codec, not just AV1/Xe_LPM_plus_base.

Added all 167 missing include directories (36 for Xe_LPM_plus_base,
131 across the other 5 variants), found by listing every directory
under each "_base" tree that actually contains a header file. No
duplicates introduced (verified).

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 Android.bp | 169 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 169 insertions(+)

